1
00:00:20,854 --> 00:00:25,692
‎30 MILES NORTH OF THE MIDPOINT
‎RED CANYON

2
00:00:36,911 --> 00:00:37,996
‎There it is.

3
00:00:42,625 --> 00:00:45,252
‎That's the Zombie Horse?

4
00:00:45,253 --> 00:00:48,965
‎It's just a lousy mural
‎of a vicious-looking horse.

5
00:01:02,979 --> 00:01:04,606
‎What are you doing with that?

6
00:01:06,232 --> 00:01:08,818
‎Johnny, do you have any wire?

7
00:01:12,363 --> 00:01:14,574
‎Hey! What the hell are you doing?

8
00:01:15,283 --> 00:01:17,493
‎The Zombie Horse heals injuries.

9
00:01:17,494 --> 00:01:19,578
‎This must be for stitching.

10
00:01:19,579 --> 00:01:20,955
‎My father was a doctor.

11
00:01:21,539 --> 00:01:22,707
‎A doctor?

12
00:01:23,958 --> 00:01:26,752
‎This thread can heal injuries,
‎up to a point.

13
00:01:26,753 --> 00:01:30,380
‎It'll even reattach flesh
‎that's been blown off.

14
00:01:30,381 --> 00:01:34,803
‎How does that even work?
‎There's no way!

15
00:01:35,678 --> 00:01:38,514
‎But if it really can heal...

16
00:01:38,515 --> 00:01:41,601
‎Like the Steel Ball, it's something more.

17
00:01:42,977 --> 00:01:45,104
‎Like a Stand ability.

18
00:01:48,024 --> 00:01:49,025
‎No.

19
00:01:49,609 --> 00:01:53,363
‎Just like the letter said,
‎it's a gift from the king.

20
00:01:54,072 --> 00:01:57,617
‎My father never writes letters.

21
00:01:58,868 --> 00:02:01,246
‎An executioner and a doctor.

22
00:02:01,746 --> 00:02:03,915
‎Even if I asked him about it,

23
00:02:04,499 --> 00:02:06,334
‎he'd never tell me.

24
00:02:08,253 --> 00:02:11,589
‎1875 KINGDOM OF NAPLES

25
00:02:19,347 --> 00:02:20,807
‎Good morning, sir.

26
00:02:22,892 --> 00:02:26,187
‎Gyro Zeppeli. How old are you now?

27
00:02:26,771 --> 00:02:27,981
‎I'm nine, sir.

28
00:02:42,537 --> 00:02:44,789
‎STEEL BALL RUN
‎JOJO'S BIZARRE ADVENTURE

29
00:03:59,572 --> 00:04:03,409
‎#06
‎GYRO ZEPPELI’S DESTINY

30
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:06,411
‎I'm off to the castle.

31
00:04:06,412 --> 00:04:07,913
‎Take care, dear.

32
00:04:07,914 --> 00:04:09,665
‎Listen, Gyro.

33
00:04:09,666 --> 00:04:12,251
‎Every man needs a map.

34
00:04:12,252 --> 00:04:15,629
‎A map in his heart to guide him
‎across the wilderness.

35
00:04:15,630 --> 00:04:18,883
‎-Never forget that.
‎-Yes, Father.

36
00:04:19,467 --> 00:04:22,928
‎Gregorio Zeppeli, Gyro Zeppeli's father.

37
00:04:22,929 --> 00:04:25,682
‎He was a doctor.

38
00:04:26,391 --> 00:04:30,352
‎He treated the rich and the poor alike

39
00:04:30,353 --> 00:04:32,730
‎at his family clinic.

40
00:04:37,068 --> 00:04:41,698
‎Gyro, how would you get the Steel Ball
‎out of my fist?

41
00:04:47,078 --> 00:04:50,497
‎Ow! Not like that, Gyro!

42
00:04:50,498 --> 00:04:53,041
‎I'm talking about the Spin!

43
00:04:53,042 --> 00:04:57,422
‎I'm asking how you'd get it out
‎using the Spin.

44
00:04:58,881 --> 00:05:01,175
‎That's impossible, Father.

45
00:05:01,718 --> 00:05:03,302
‎Listen, Gyro.

46
00:05:03,303 --> 00:05:06,013
‎You spend all your time riding horses,

47
00:05:06,014 --> 00:05:11,269
‎but you must master the Spin
‎by the time you're 13.

48
00:05:14,230 --> 00:05:17,859
‎The Spin is the source of all power.

49
00:05:18,401 --> 00:05:20,986
‎My father taught me.

50
00:05:20,987 --> 00:05:24,364
‎His father taught him too.

51
00:05:24,365 --> 00:05:25,741
‎Why?

52
00:05:25,742 --> 00:05:29,746
‎What's the connection
‎between the Steel Ball and our family?

53
00:05:30,330 --> 00:05:33,790
‎Because every man in the Zeppeli family
‎has done so.

54
00:05:33,791 --> 00:05:35,710
‎I know you can do it.

55
00:05:37,337 --> 00:05:38,670
‎You may go now.

56
00:05:38,671 --> 00:05:39,672
‎Yes, Father.

57
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:45,052
‎Putting it in a fist

58
00:05:45,053 --> 00:05:47,847
‎is easier than taking it out.

59
00:05:50,183 --> 00:05:52,143
‎No way! When did he...

60
00:05:55,354 --> 00:05:58,232
‎FOUR YEARS LATER

61
00:06:01,152 --> 00:06:03,279
‎Gyro. How old are you now?

62
00:06:05,823 --> 00:06:07,325
‎I'm 13, sir.

63
00:06:08,785 --> 00:06:11,036
‎I'm off to the castle.

64
00:06:11,037 --> 00:06:12,455
‎Take care, dear.

65
00:06:13,122 --> 00:06:14,706
‎-Gyro.
‎-Yes, Father?

66
00:06:14,707 --> 00:06:17,627
‎You're coming with me today.

67
00:06:18,669 --> 00:06:19,670
‎What?

68
00:06:29,180 --> 00:06:31,890
‎Aren't we going to the castle?

69
00:06:31,891 --> 00:06:34,143
‎We already passed it.

70
00:06:37,438 --> 00:06:38,439
‎Gyro.

71
00:06:39,524 --> 00:06:42,359
‎Every man needs a map.

72
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:45,655
‎A map in his heart to guide him
‎across the wilderness.

73
00:06:47,281 --> 00:06:50,827
‎Listen well. You're the eldest son
‎of the Zeppeli family.

74
00:06:51,452 --> 00:06:53,995
‎You must protect your family.

75
00:06:53,996 --> 00:06:57,916
‎A person's happiness
‎lies within their family.

76
00:06:57,917 --> 00:07:01,878
‎Protecting your family
‎means protecting your country.

77
00:07:01,879 --> 00:07:04,923
‎If a family falls apart,

78
00:07:04,924 --> 00:07:09,636
‎you dishonor both your ancestors
‎and your descendants.

79
00:07:09,637 --> 00:07:11,513
‎Never forget that.

80
00:07:11,514 --> 00:07:12,557
‎Yes, Father.

81
00:07:21,149 --> 00:07:22,358
‎This place is...

82
00:07:24,610 --> 00:07:28,196
‎Starting today,
‎you'll assist me with my work.

83
00:07:28,197 --> 00:07:30,907
‎Your work as a doctor?

84
00:07:30,908 --> 00:07:34,077
‎This duty was entrusted to us

85
00:07:34,078 --> 00:07:37,248
‎380 years ago by the king.

86
00:07:37,748 --> 00:07:41,585
‎It has been the Zeppeli family's duty
‎ever since.

87
00:07:41,586 --> 00:07:44,338
‎It has endured through every king's reign.

88
00:07:45,006 --> 00:07:47,632
‎Approach it with the utmost solemnity.

89
00:07:47,633 --> 00:07:51,219
‎Judicial Official!
‎Please come to the courtyard!

90
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:52,554
‎No!

91
00:07:52,555 --> 00:07:55,849
‎-He's out of control. Thrashing about!
‎-Damn you all!

92
00:07:55,850 --> 00:07:59,895
‎Where's the priest?
‎Couldn't he prepare him for this?

93
00:07:59,896 --> 00:08:01,230
‎We can't handle the convict.

94
00:08:02,148 --> 00:08:04,984
‎He has no peace of mind.

95
00:08:06,110 --> 00:08:07,111
‎Gyro.

96
00:08:07,612 --> 00:08:10,948
‎Wait here. I'll tell you what to do.

97
00:08:22,376 --> 00:08:23,544
‎Father!

98
00:08:26,547 --> 00:08:28,048
‎Stop!

99
00:08:28,049 --> 00:08:31,092
‎No! I don't wanna die!

100
00:08:31,093 --> 00:08:32,469
‎I don't wanna die!

101
00:08:32,470 --> 00:08:35,932
‎-Don't move. Quiet your mind.
‎-Damn you!

102
00:08:36,933 --> 00:08:39,684
‎I don't wanna die! Stop!

103
00:08:39,685 --> 00:08:40,728
‎Quiet your mind...

104
00:09:20,059 --> 00:09:22,979
‎You will cleanse the sword.

105
00:09:24,272 --> 00:09:27,483
‎Your duty begins here.

106
00:09:33,573 --> 00:09:35,533
‎Yes, Father.

107
00:09:40,663 --> 00:09:43,623
‎Wherever capital punishment
‎is upheld by law,

108
00:09:43,624 --> 00:09:47,253
‎someone must carry it out.

109
00:09:47,962 --> 00:09:52,924
‎An executioner must know
‎the human body inside and out.

110
00:09:52,925 --> 00:09:57,555
‎The Zeppeli ancestors studied medicine
‎and mastered the art of combat.

111
00:09:58,306 --> 00:10:01,641
‎They also created the Spin

112
00:10:01,642 --> 00:10:04,269
‎to keep the body at peace.

113
00:10:04,270 --> 00:10:06,980
‎The Spin exists not for pain,

114
00:10:06,981 --> 00:10:09,274
‎but for peace.

115
00:10:09,275 --> 00:10:12,153
‎Each generation refined it further.

116
00:10:13,070 --> 00:10:14,738
‎Carrying out executions.

117
00:10:14,739 --> 00:10:19,492
‎That is the Zeppeli family's destiny
‎for the past 380 years.

118
00:10:19,493 --> 00:10:23,122
‎12 YEARS LATER

119
00:10:23,873 --> 00:10:26,041
‎Stay back, you bastard!

120
00:10:26,042 --> 00:10:30,420
‎If I'm dying, I'm taking
‎as many of you with me as I can!

121
00:10:30,421 --> 00:10:33,007
‎One step closer and I'll kill him!

122
00:10:34,133 --> 00:10:35,843
‎Help me!

123
00:10:41,474 --> 00:10:43,934
‎Are you crazy?

124
00:10:54,528 --> 00:10:57,781
‎It's twisting... It's tightening!

125
00:10:57,782 --> 00:10:59,449
‎Get him!

126
00:10:59,450 --> 00:11:01,493
‎You bastard!

127
00:11:01,494 --> 00:11:02,828
‎Well done, Gyro!

128
00:11:03,412 --> 00:11:05,790
‎Just like Mr. Zeppeli's son!

129
00:11:11,045 --> 00:11:13,673
‎Gyro. How old are you now?

130
00:11:15,591 --> 00:11:17,093
‎I'm 24, sir.

131
00:11:17,802 --> 00:11:21,262
‎When Gyro Zeppeli turned 25,

132
00:11:21,263 --> 00:11:25,308
‎he was to inherit his father's position.

133
00:11:25,309 --> 00:11:27,310
‎As his successor.

134
00:11:27,311 --> 00:11:30,980
‎Everything was as it should be.

135
00:11:30,981 --> 00:11:32,691
‎Had things stayed that way.

136
00:11:34,735 --> 00:11:39,615
‎That was until a boy named Marco,
‎who polished shoes at a noble estate...

137
00:11:40,366 --> 00:11:41,826
‎Sentenced to death.

138
00:11:43,119 --> 00:11:44,202
‎BOY SENTENCED TO DEATH
‎TREASON

139
00:11:44,203 --> 00:11:46,497
‎...was sentenced to death.

140
00:11:52,044 --> 00:11:53,379
‎Excuse me...

141
00:11:54,296 --> 00:11:55,339
‎What?

142
00:11:56,006 --> 00:11:58,258
‎Is there anything I can do?

143
00:11:58,259 --> 00:11:59,717
‎Something you can do?

144
00:11:59,718 --> 00:12:01,845
‎I want to work.

145
00:12:01,846 --> 00:12:05,515
‎When I went to serve
‎as a live-in servant for the baron,

146
00:12:05,516 --> 00:12:06,933
‎my father told me.

147
00:12:06,934 --> 00:12:09,227
‎He said if I stayed humble
‎and worked hard,

148
00:12:09,228 --> 00:12:11,604
‎I'd earn their respect someday.

149
00:12:11,605 --> 00:12:13,315
‎He said I'd find happiness.

150
00:12:14,859 --> 00:12:19,821
‎My grandfather did this work,
‎and so did his father.

151
00:12:19,822 --> 00:12:22,031
‎I can sew anything.

152
00:12:22,032 --> 00:12:24,410
‎No one shines shoes better than me.

153
00:12:24,994 --> 00:12:27,496
‎I can polish silverware until it shines.

154
00:12:28,581 --> 00:12:32,834
‎I can memorize every dish
‎and every wine, and--

155
00:12:32,835 --> 00:12:34,211
‎That's enough! Stop!

156
00:12:37,506 --> 00:12:41,718
‎Whatever it is, I'll do it carefully.
‎I'll do it well.

157
00:12:41,719 --> 00:12:43,219
‎Just like my father said--

158
00:12:43,220 --> 00:12:44,555
‎Don't talk to me!

159
00:12:46,140 --> 00:12:47,766
‎Never again. Got it?

160
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:53,564
‎Never again...

161
00:12:58,444 --> 00:13:01,446
‎JUDICIAL OFFICIAL ZEPPELI
‎CHALLENGED THE BOY'S GUILTY VERDICT

162
00:13:01,447 --> 00:13:03,448
‎BUT TO NO AVAIL

163
00:13:03,449 --> 00:13:06,451
‎You've overstepped, Gyro.

164
00:13:06,452 --> 00:13:10,371
‎All you've done is throw the country
‎into turmoil.

165
00:13:10,372 --> 00:13:15,210
‎Our family's duty isn't to decide
‎guilt or innocence.

166
00:13:15,211 --> 00:13:19,130
‎Father, I only want to be convinced
‎this is just.

167
00:13:19,131 --> 00:13:21,591
‎Personal conviction has no place here!

168
00:13:21,592 --> 00:13:25,012
‎Not even for the vilest criminals.

169
00:13:25,596 --> 00:13:28,348
‎But that boy...

170
00:13:28,349 --> 00:13:32,728
‎He had nothing to do
‎with the plot of his employer, the baron.

171
00:13:33,312 --> 00:13:35,104
‎He only polished shoes.

172
00:13:35,105 --> 00:13:40,235
‎We carry out the king's orders.
‎Nothing more.

173
00:13:40,236 --> 00:13:43,738
‎The law is the law.
‎Stay out of the legal process.

174
00:13:43,739 --> 00:13:46,449
‎It is beyond personal conviction.

175
00:13:46,450 --> 00:13:48,577
‎All is God's will!

176
00:13:49,828 --> 00:13:52,248
‎He has been sentenced to death.

177
00:13:53,582 --> 00:13:55,917
‎Soon I'll turn 25

178
00:13:55,918 --> 00:13:57,753
‎and succeed you.

179
00:13:58,337 --> 00:14:03,092
‎Will my first duty be to behead
‎that nine-year-old boy?

180
00:14:06,804 --> 00:14:09,889
‎I never made friends.

181
00:14:09,890 --> 00:14:11,724
‎I don't keep pets.

182
00:14:11,725 --> 00:14:14,310
‎I dine only with my family.

183
00:14:14,311 --> 00:14:17,522
‎I don't even invite relatives
‎into my home.

184
00:14:17,523 --> 00:14:21,569
‎I never keep a diary or write letters.

185
00:14:22,152 --> 00:14:27,115
‎If my hand were off
‎by even a tenth of a millimeter,

186
00:14:27,116 --> 00:14:30,660
‎the execution would fail.

187
00:14:30,661 --> 00:14:35,374
‎Worse, it would inflict
‎unimaginable suffering on the condemned.

188
00:14:38,586 --> 00:14:42,505
‎That's caused by sentiment.

189
00:14:42,506 --> 00:14:43,756
‎Sentiment...

190
00:14:43,757 --> 00:14:47,886
‎Personal ties lead to sentiment.

191
00:14:47,887 --> 00:14:50,723
‎Sentiment leaves your heart vulnerable.

192
00:14:52,016 --> 00:14:53,142
‎My son.

193
00:14:53,726 --> 00:14:56,519
‎A sentimental heart is dangerous.

194
00:14:56,520 --> 00:14:59,148
‎It can make your future miserable.

195
00:14:59,732 --> 00:15:01,984
‎Never forget, my son.

196
00:15:04,820 --> 00:15:09,574
‎High treason
‎was the gravest of all crimes.

197
00:15:09,575 --> 00:15:13,078
‎Even a boy who did nothing
‎but polish shoes...

198
00:15:13,662 --> 00:15:18,208
‎Such was the law of that nation
‎in those days.

199
00:15:41,649 --> 00:15:44,568
‎TWO MONTHS EARLIER

200
00:15:51,283 --> 00:15:53,494
‎"All is God's will."

201
00:15:54,119 --> 00:15:55,329
‎Is it really?

202
00:15:58,207 --> 00:16:00,876
‎Gyro. How old are you now?

203
00:16:02,002 --> 00:16:04,004
‎You already know that.

204
00:16:06,048 --> 00:16:08,883
‎So why did you send for me?

205
00:16:08,884 --> 00:16:11,010
‎Need advice or something?

206
00:16:11,011 --> 00:16:13,346
‎Then ask someone else.

207
00:16:13,347 --> 00:16:16,350
‎Aren't you the one
‎who's got something on your mind?

208
00:16:16,976 --> 00:16:19,268
‎About the boy.

209
00:16:19,269 --> 00:16:20,729
‎The boy...

210
00:16:22,898 --> 00:16:25,358
‎I'm proud of my family,

211
00:16:25,359 --> 00:16:27,026
‎and I'll succeed my father.

212
00:16:27,027 --> 00:16:29,737
‎This duty is my destiny.

213
00:16:29,738 --> 00:16:31,448
‎That'll never change.

214
00:16:32,574 --> 00:16:34,993
‎It never has, and it never will.

215
00:16:34,994 --> 00:16:36,912
‎But I...

216
00:16:40,082 --> 00:16:42,126
‎I just want to be convinced!

217
00:16:42,751 --> 00:16:47,213
‎I want this duty from the king
‎to be a source of pride.

218
00:16:47,214 --> 00:16:51,175
‎I have to be convinced!
‎That's where my pride comes from!

219
00:16:51,176 --> 00:16:53,511
‎I'd give my life for that pride!

220
00:16:53,512 --> 00:16:56,055
‎High treason is a grave crime.

221
00:16:56,056 --> 00:16:58,142
‎But laws can be wrong.

222
00:16:58,726 --> 00:17:03,688
‎I can't accept an uninvolved boy
‎being condemned to death!

223
00:17:03,689 --> 00:17:06,400
‎I have to be convinced it's just!

224
00:17:07,192 --> 00:17:11,320
‎Would you risk your life for that boy?

225
00:17:11,321 --> 00:17:12,864
‎Is that what you're saying?

226
00:17:12,865 --> 00:17:14,490
‎I want to be sure.

227
00:17:14,491 --> 00:17:15,575
‎What?

228
00:17:15,576 --> 00:17:17,827
‎Let me ask you again.

229
00:17:17,828 --> 00:17:20,496
‎If that boy could be cleared,

230
00:17:20,497 --> 00:17:22,458
‎would you risk your life?

231
00:17:23,167 --> 00:17:25,752
‎What the hell are you talking about?

232
00:17:25,753 --> 00:17:27,087
‎Can you?

233
00:17:33,343 --> 00:17:35,679
‎Yes. I want to save him.

234
00:17:37,931 --> 00:17:40,392
‎He only polished shoes.

235
00:17:41,018 --> 00:17:44,396
‎Is it foolish for a Zeppeli man
‎to feel this way?

236
00:17:44,897 --> 00:17:48,442
‎There's only one way
‎to overturn the sentence.

237
00:17:49,234 --> 00:17:51,778
‎If a war were to break out,

238
00:17:51,779 --> 00:17:53,946
‎and the Kingdom emerged victorious...

239
00:17:53,947 --> 00:17:59,578
‎The king must grant a royal pardon
‎for a kingdom-wide celebration.

240
00:18:00,746 --> 00:18:04,541
‎A royal pardon is an act of clemency
‎that reduces a criminal's sentence!

241
00:18:05,167 --> 00:18:07,251
‎A royal pardon?

242
00:18:07,252 --> 00:18:09,754
‎Yes. He will definitely issue one.

243
00:18:09,755 --> 00:18:12,173
‎No! That's not my point.

244
00:18:12,174 --> 00:18:14,468
‎Where would a war even break out?

245
00:18:15,719 --> 00:18:17,346
‎"The Steel Ball Run"...

246
00:18:18,305 --> 00:18:21,850
‎You've mastered the Steel Ball technique,
‎Gyro Zeppeli!

247
00:18:22,518 --> 00:18:25,353
‎You can win it.
‎That's why I'm telling you this.

248
00:18:25,354 --> 00:18:29,774
‎The whole world sees winning this race
‎as the equivalent

249
00:18:29,775 --> 00:18:32,361
‎of winning a war!

250
00:18:32,861 --> 00:18:35,321
‎If a rider from our Kingdom wins,

251
00:18:35,322 --> 00:18:38,867
‎our king will grant a royal pardon!

252
00:18:41,078 --> 00:18:43,538
‎This is my map.

253
00:18:43,539 --> 00:18:47,167
‎The map in my heart to guide me
‎across the wilderness!

254
00:18:58,595 --> 00:19:00,596
‎Only 15 miles to the finish.

255
00:19:00,597 --> 00:19:03,307
‎Just because there aren't any officials...
‎That bastard!

256
00:19:03,308 --> 00:19:06,269
‎That terrorist
‎is seventh in the first stage...

257
00:19:06,270 --> 00:19:08,437
‎Fritz von Stroheim, from Germany!

258
00:19:08,438 --> 00:19:09,897
‎You know him too?

259
00:19:09,898 --> 00:19:13,443
‎No. Nobody I know has hair like that.

260
00:19:13,944 --> 00:19:15,821
‎He's coming again, Gyro!

261
00:19:19,324 --> 00:19:20,450
‎Gyro!

262
00:19:31,378 --> 00:19:34,256
‎It hurts!

263
00:19:37,176 --> 00:19:40,887
‎Damn! Who the hell are you?

264
00:19:40,888 --> 00:19:42,930
‎The Spin of the Steel Ball...

265
00:19:42,931 --> 00:19:45,224
‎They can grind away matter

266
00:19:45,225 --> 00:19:47,810
‎and even control human muscles.

267
00:19:47,811 --> 00:19:52,023
‎They can even harden your skin
‎enough to stop bullets, huh?

268
00:19:52,024 --> 00:19:53,400
‎You...

269
00:19:54,943 --> 00:19:56,277
‎Gyro!

270
00:19:56,278 --> 00:19:59,155
‎Drop them, Gyro Zeppeli!

271
00:19:59,156 --> 00:20:01,532
‎Drop the Steel Ball right now

272
00:20:01,533 --> 00:20:05,870
‎or your friend and your horse are next.

273
00:20:05,871 --> 00:20:08,497
‎Or you can throw them at me if you like.

274
00:20:08,498 --> 00:20:12,377
‎Then I'll prove my gun's faster.

275
00:20:13,170 --> 00:20:16,589
‎Drop them? My Steel Ball?

276
00:20:16,590 --> 00:20:18,967
‎You sure you want that?

277
00:20:20,052 --> 00:20:23,387
‎If you're that determined,

278
00:20:23,388 --> 00:20:25,766
‎then I really will.

279
00:20:32,689 --> 00:20:33,899
‎There. I let go.

280
00:20:51,416 --> 00:20:52,584
‎Terrorists...

281
00:20:53,585 --> 00:20:57,005
‎Just what kind of country are you from?

282
00:20:58,048 --> 00:21:03,302
‎Even if winning this race
‎symbolizes national glory,

283
00:21:03,303 --> 00:21:04,429
‎this is too much!

284
00:21:05,264 --> 00:21:07,848
‎Why do they keep coming after you?

285
00:21:07,849 --> 00:21:09,934
‎They're only after you.

286
00:21:09,935 --> 00:21:11,686
‎It's just a race!

287
00:21:11,687 --> 00:21:13,980
‎I feel like there's something deeper...

288
00:21:13,981 --> 00:21:18,485
‎some old feud
‎between the terrorists and your country.

289
00:21:21,446 --> 00:21:23,532
‎I serve the king.

290
00:21:24,116 --> 00:21:26,909
‎If I win, he will grant a royal pardon.

291
00:21:26,910 --> 00:21:28,327
‎That's all.

292
00:21:28,328 --> 00:21:29,787
‎A royal pardon?

293
00:21:29,788 --> 00:21:33,332
‎I'm crossing this continent
‎in first place.

294
00:21:33,333 --> 00:21:36,002
‎If you think this is too dangerous,

295
00:21:36,003 --> 00:21:38,463
‎you'd better go your own way.

296
00:21:44,970 --> 00:21:47,264
‎I must have been hurt when I fell off.

297
00:21:48,140 --> 00:21:50,058
‎But I don't feel any pain.

298
00:23:30,951 --> 00:23:35,956
‎Subtitle translation by: Ryoko Quirke
